cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dataset-integrity-audit"
message: "If you use this tool or its measurements, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ashish
    family-names: Sinha
    email: sinha.ashish.4.u@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/ashishsinha1602/dataset-integrity-audit"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible integrity audit for Hugging Face datasets. Validates schema,
  flags degenerate records, and measures duplication three ways: exact matches
  on the natural-language field, exact matches on the reference answer, and
  near-duplicates by shingle Jaccard with MinHash-LSH above 3,000 records.
  Near-duplicate clusters are separated into records identical across every
  evaluated field and records that merely share a question stem, because
  conflating the two overstates duplication roughly ninefold on Spider's
  training split. Also measures cross-split contamination, where requiring the
  reference answer to match alongside the question reduces the apparent
  contamination rate threefold.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - data-quality
  - contamination
  - deduplication
  - llm-evaluation
license: MIT
